WEBVTT

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:20.680
Margaret, the Lancastrian queen, has
raised troops and conquered the north.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:25.190
I will march north and settle
matters with her myself.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.900
Edward, take charge of the Welsh border.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.110
Yes, Father!

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:35.200
Earl of Warwick, defend London for me.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.070
Yes, Majesty.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.370
Father!

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.450
Take me with you! I won't be a burden!

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.050
Richard.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.170
Father.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.170
My love!

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.300
Please, leave me Richard!

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.850
Don't take my little Richard from me!

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.730
I know he will go off to war someday,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:09.860
but he is still too delicate now.
He needs his mother.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:15.700
Please! Please have pity on
a foolish woman's whim!

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.330
Richard, I won't be gone long.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.950
Guard your mother until I return.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.250
Father.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.430
I'll never let you go to him.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:42.010
Your existence will be the death of him.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:45.930
Your words become curses
that bring others to ruin.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.190
You filthy demon child!

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:51.560
You cannot live without
devouring the souls of others!

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.400
O Lord, I will guard them
all from this devil.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.030
That shall be my penance
for giving birth to him!

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.710
York of the white rose.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:12.340
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:18.760
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.510
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:05.030
The Lancastrian stronghold is under our
noses! Keep your swords in hand!

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.620
Fortune favors us!

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:19.130
This can't be all of Margaret's forces.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.220
They must have run in fear of our army.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:27.390
Something's not right.
How can our enemy number so few?

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.730
It's almost Christmas, huh?

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:45.570
I guess a big family celebration
is out of the question, considering.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.660
Say, Mother, where has Richard gone?

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.620
I sent him to a safe place.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.130
To the Tower.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.710
Are there prisoners in the Tower?
Apart from me, I mean.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:06.260
Prisoners? Goodness, no!
There are only noble personages here.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:08.800
Noble prisoners, then.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.560
Of course.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.430
Henry must be here.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:17.190
If I weren't locked up,
I'd kill him at once

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.610
and race to my father's side
with his head!

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:23.360
York was quite a disappointment.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.030
Is this all he amounts to
without Warwick and Edward?

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.450
Your Majesty! We will secure your escape!

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:33.330
What king would sacrifice his men
to save only his own skin?

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.290
But Your Majesty!

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:41.210
I swore an oath to stand my ground.
It's a crown or an honorable death for me!

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.430
Lancaster!

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.350
A king...

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:03.940
A king stands firm! He never retreats!

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.360
I swore it by my name!

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:15.250
I swore it to you, Richard!

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.880
Richard, everyone who
passes under this tree

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.800
must kiss whoever is
near them at the time.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.260
Is that true?

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.850
So, even Mother won't
get mad if I kiss her?

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.180
Of course she won't!

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.890
But the rule is that you must
do it at least 12 times,

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.810
so kiss me first.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:39.940
Father!

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.810
Father!

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.820
Richard?

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:55.450
Oh, good. You're still alive.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:07:00.460
Hurry up and kill me.
I have only moments of life left.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.000
No, Your Majesty.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.380
I kept you alive to disgrace you.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:10.970
Now, put this on. I worked hard
to weave it specially for you.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:15.970
Look, Your Majesty.
It's the "crown" you so longed for.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.650
Dear me.

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:25.690
How it becomes you!

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:28.030
Come, gentlemen! Salute him!

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.660
This isn't the end.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:37.240
You must entertain me more before you die,

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.870
York.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.750
Go on! Keep struggling!
Lose your composure!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:48.250
My wrath won't be sated until
the world sees your disgrace!

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:52.680
Even if I die, wings of vengeance

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:56.390
will rise again from my ashes.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:08:00.430
So, that hope is the source
of your noble bearing.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.390
I've heard the stories.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:06.650
Edward the womanizer.
George the simpleton.

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.730
And then there's your youngest.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:14.320
I hear you lavish your affections
on that little boy most of all.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:15.990
What are you scheming?

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.580
"Scheming"? Perish the thought.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:22.870
I merely wanted you to have this
in your last moments, Your Majesty.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:26.250
Here you are.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.550
Take a good look, York.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:35.180
I wrung the blood that stains this cloth
from your beloved youngest son's heart.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.590
Richard!

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:43.560
Go on. Wipe your tears with it.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.920
Yes! That's the look I wanted!

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.460
I wanted to see your handsome
face twisted in despair!

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:13.420
Poor, pitiful York!

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:16.630
All right, I've had my fun.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:22.560
Now, despair and die.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:27.100
Your Lordship, we can't hold out here!

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.610
Send the rearguard south!
I'll lead the main force!

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.150
Hold London at any cost!

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:37.280
Prince Edward! It appears that they've
already moved His Majesty, King Henry.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.660
My queen,

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:50.090
I recaptured King Henry in transit
and took him under my protection.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.800
Well done.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.090
Take all that your hearts desire!

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.170
We will continue our advance.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:02.930
Next time, I'll wipe York's head
with his son's <i>real </i>blood.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.280
Father.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:22.620
Where am I?! What are you doing here?!

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:25.160
This is a Lancastrian subject's house,

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.830
and you're a prisoner in my custody.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:31.420
We'll stay here temporarily until
I can join my mother's army.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:36.340
Margaret's army? You mean
the Lancastrians are advancing?

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.680
You don't know anything?

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.010
Not even that your father is--

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:45.390
What about my father?!
Did something happen to him?!

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:50.940
Your father is in the city of York.
It's too far to go alone.

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:53.150
I wouldn't mind taking you there,

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:55.730
if you'll agree to stay with me.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:58.650
What should I stay with
a Lancastrian for?!

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:03.530
If I go to see my father, I'll do it
with my mother and brother.

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:08.830
I hear that your mother already took
your brother and fled, Richard.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.790
They abandoned you.

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:17.510
Mother?

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:27.180
It wouldn't be the first time
I was abandoned.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:35.230
Hang on! Our troops will
capture this area soon!

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:36.860
Why stop me?

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:40.780
I've been abandoned; that makes
me worthless as a hostage.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.240
Well...

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.660
I don't know why either,

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:47.620
b-but I think it's because you're a woman!

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.790
I'm not a woman.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:54.000
My father called me his son.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.250
He named me "Richard."

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:08.430
Damn it. Which way should I go?

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.480
I have to reach Father soon!

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.480
Hey.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.730
What are you doing there?

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:17.400
We Lancastrians have occupied this town.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:26.200
Most of the townsfolk have fled.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.160
Think. Think, Richard.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.370
It's a long way to York.

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.000
You need a horse.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.540
If the Lancastrians have taken the town,
then getting out won't be easy.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:39.840
You don't know anything?

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.970
Not even that your father is--

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:45.390
I have to reach Father soon!

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:48.890
Are you really from this town?

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.350
Father!

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:55.980
I need to reach you soon!

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.660
Come off already, damn it!

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:13.370
Hurry up and come off!

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.690
A wife and children.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:46.360
He's these children's father...

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:50.200
...and I killed him.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:12.850
Father!

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.230
Who's that over there?

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:24.320
O Lord! Richard!

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:25.990
Is it really you?

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:33.200
I'm so glad.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.660
I thought I'd never see you again.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.160
Why?

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:41.170
Why did you have to turn up
at a time like this?!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:45.300
What have you been doing all this time?
What brings you here?

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.300
Stay back!

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.880
Stay back!

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:50.260
All right.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:53.430
In that case, Richard, you come to me.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.640
I've been longing to see you.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:59.480
Who asked you?

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:03.190
I made up my mind to go it alone.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.570
All alone.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.240
I have to go alone, and yet...!

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.110
Wait! Richard!

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:12.530
Let go of me! I don't have time for your--

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.200
I want to go with you!

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:16.790
Won't you take me along?!

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.000
You?

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.460
What... What do you want
to come with me for?

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:24.420
I want to be with you.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:28.800
When I'm with you,
I feel as though I can be myself.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:32.090
That's why I want to go back
to that forest with you.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:39.480
Then, I want to spend every day tending
sheep and obeying the church bells.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:42.270
I want to live in peace and quiet.

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:46.190
Wouldn't a life like that spare
you from getting hurt like this?

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.190
Hurt?

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.820
I'm not hurt at all.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.580
This is...

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:57.160
...someone else's blood.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:02.000
I'm not like you.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.080
If you're not hurt,

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:06.670
then why are you crying?

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.510
I...

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:10.380
I don't need anyone.

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:13.720
Richard!

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:16.220
Your Majesty!

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:19.600
I've been looking for you.

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:23.850
Let us return to our London together.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:30.070
My father is waiting for me.

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.860
He's waiting for me.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:37.120
So, our unit is the only one left.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:40.790
Fighting on won't do us much good
now that the main force is gone.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.620
It's too soon to give up!

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:45.210
Edward's forces are coming to our aid!

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:48.040
Whatever happens,
we must hold out until he arrives!

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:03.060
I won't let His Majesty's dream--
<i>my </i>dream--come to an end yet!

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.350
Father.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:17.030
Which road will take me to York?

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.910
It's that way, direction-wise.

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.080
Hey.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:25.540
Are you all right? You don't look well,
and York's a long way off.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:28.340
I don't have time to rest.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:29.960
Is that so?

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.630
Watch out for robbers, then.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:38.680
Behold, Your Majesty.

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:41.260
Could anything be more delightful?

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:44.350
It's a shame that Warwick's
corpse is lacking,

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:46.730
but York, who tried to
steal your crown, is--

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.980
I don't want to hear about that!

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.820
Oh, how horrible!

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:53.530
I made a covenant with the Duke of York,

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.070
and now it's come to this!

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.280
That's true, isn't it, Your Majesty?

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:06.330
You ceded the throne to York and his sons.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:09.000
Tell me, Your Majesty:

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:13.960
What outrage cost your son his place
in the line of succession?

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.380
Tell him in person.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.510
Mother!

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:20.600
Father would never disinherit me.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:24.100
Everyone knows that the
king's son will be the next king!

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:25.730
Of course.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:29.190
Even the lowliest beast
cares for its young.

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:32.570
That's why the sight of
enemies frightens them.

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:34.980
Now, look! Look, Henry!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:38.910
Look at the soldiers you killed!
At the son you abandoned!

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:41.950
It's not my fault! I couldn't help it!

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.620
I couldn't help it!

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:47.370
I just didn't want anyone to die!

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.290
Forgive me! Forgive me!

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.630
What a cowardly, contemptible,
shameless king.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:59.760
I wish that I had never become your wife.

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:03.050
Oh, my darling William.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:05.720
You no longer have a body to embrace,

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:09.940
and you took my heart with you to heaven.

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.480
I'm sorry.

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:14.150
Forgive me, York.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:17.780
Forgive me. Forgive me.

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:20.530
Damn. I drove the horse too hard.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.040
I hate forests at night.

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:02.070
The Lancastrians must have
ransacked this house.

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:10.160
Father, I hope that you
have hot food to eat.

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:13.500
Is someone there?

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:22.880
A deserter from the
Lancastrian army, are you?

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:27.470
He'll make a perfect mark.
Hurry up and strip him down.

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:29.430
Don't try anything, kid!

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:32.190
You sons of bitches did
a number on our village!

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.480
Hey, this brat's a woman.

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:37.900
We're in luck.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:38.900
No.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.440
I'm not a woman!

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.400
Stop! Stop!

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.570
Father!

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:46.570
What is this brat?

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:55.250
I'm not a woman.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.960
Father, save me!

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.460
Demon child! Demon child!

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:01.510
You're wrong!

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:03.340
I'm not a demon child!

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:06.970
I'm my father's son!

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:11.180
Only my father will save me
from the darkness.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:35.290
Father!

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:52.560
Father.

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:58.270
My light.
